A file manager's drag is pointer input: its enter, its moves and its drop put the window in mouse input mode, as a
mouse move or press does. Before this, typed keys kept the window in keyboard mode through the drag, so no hitbox was
hovered and a drop reached no `on_drop` listener: the files went nowhere, though the source was told the drop was
done. A key after the drop puts the window back in keyboard mode. `tests/file_drop_input_mode.rs` tests it (the crate's
own `--lib` tests do not build from the crates.io package). An upstream candidate (Zed).

